DXWEB AND DXWEB ADMIN - INSTALLATION AND UPGRADES
=================================================

This document explains how to install and upgrade DXWeb and DXWeb Admin
as components of the DXSpider source tree.

The standard installation runs the applications directly, without a
reverse proxy. Reverse proxies are NOT officially supported. Nginx is
included here only as a real-world configuration example. This does not
imply support for Nginx or for any other reverse proxy.

Run the commands as root. Docker is not required.

The recommended service account is user sysop and group spider.
You may choose another existing Unix user and group if preferred.
Replace --user and --group consistently in every command below.
The root account used to run the installer is separate from the
account used to run the applications.

FILE LOCATIONS
--------------

  /spider/INSTALL_DXWEB      This document
  /spider/dxweb/             DXWeb and its installer
  /spider/dxweb-admin/       DXWeb Admin

Both applications are part of the DXSpider Git repository. Application
updates arrive when that repository is updated. The installer configures
services and, where requested, the Nginx example; it does not copy the
application source files over themselves.

1. COMMON PREPARATION
---------------------

Log in to the DXSpider server as root and run:

  cd /spider
  pwd
  git status --short
  ls -ld dxweb dxweb-admin
  ls -l dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl
  perl -c dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --help

Stop if a required file is missing or the syntax check fails.

2. FIRST INSTALLATION WITHOUT NGINX
-----------------------------------

This configuration exposes DXWeb on port 7380 and DXWeb Admin on 7381.

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components both --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider

Review the files and services that would be created or changed.
If the plan is correct, apply it:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components both --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider --apply

Verify the result using section 7.

3. UPGRADING WITHOUT NGINX
--------------------------

First update DXSpider using your normal repository update procedure.
Before pulling, inspect local modifications and resolve any conflicts.
Do not discard local changes merely to continue an upgrade.

  cd /spider
  git status --short
  git pull --ff-only
  perl -c dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl

Then review the installation plan:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components both --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider

If the plan is correct, apply it:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components both --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider --apply

The install action also restarts the selected services after Git updates,
even when no service configuration changes are required.
Verify the result using section 7.

4. FIRST INSTALLATION WITH NGINX (UNSUPPORTED EXAMPLE)
------------------------------------------------------

IMPORTANT: Reverse proxies are not officially supported. The Nginx
instructions below are an example, not a supported deployment promise.
Operators are responsible for their proxy configuration, security,
certificates, compatibility, and maintenance.

In this example, Nginx serves public ports 7380 and 7381. The Perl
applications listen internally on 127.0.0.1:7480 and 127.0.0.1:7481.

Before proceeding, check Nginx and back up its configuration:

  cd /spider
  nginx -t
  ls -l /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
  mkdir -p /root/dxweb-nginx-backup
  cp -a /etc/nginx/nginx.conf /root/dxweb-nginx-backup/
  cp -a /etc/nginx/sites-available /root/dxweb-nginx-backup/
  cp -a /etc/nginx/sites-enabled /root/dxweb-nginx-backup/

Never delete or replace unrelated Nginx sites. If an existing DXWeb
Nginx configuration is not managed by this installer, stop and plan a
configuration migration instead of forcing its removal.

For HTTP, replace web.example.net with your actual DNS hostname:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components both --mode nginx --scheme http \
    --hostname web.example.net --user sysop --group spider

If the plan is correct:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components both --mode nginx --scheme http \
    --hostname web.example.net --user sysop --group spider --apply

For HTTPS, obtain a valid certificate and private key beforehand.
Replace the example hostname and certificate paths with real values:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components both --mode nginx --scheme https \
    --hostname web.example.net \
    --cert /etc/ssl/dxweb/fullchain.pem \
    --key /etc/ssl/dxweb/privkey.pem \
    --user sysop --group spider

If the plan is correct:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components both --mode nginx --scheme https \
    --hostname web.example.net \
    --cert /etc/ssl/dxweb/fullchain.pem \
    --key /etc/ssl/dxweb/privkey.pem \
    --user sysop --group spider --apply

Do not use the example certificate paths literally. The installer does
not issue certificates. Do not enable HTTPS without real credentials.

5. UPGRADING WITH NGINX (UNSUPPORTED EXAMPLE)
--------------------------------------------

Reverse proxies remain unsupported; this is an Nginx-specific example.

First update the DXSpider repository, after reviewing local changes:

  cd /spider
  git status --short
  git pull --ff-only
  perl -c dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl
  nginx -t

Back up Nginx as shown in section 4. Preserve the existing hostname,
HTTP/HTTPS scheme, and certificate paths.

For HTTP:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components both --mode nginx --scheme http \
    --hostname web.example.net --user sysop --group spider

If the plan is correct:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components both --mode nginx --scheme http \
    --hostname web.example.net --user sysop --group spider --apply

For HTTPS, repeat the HTTPS plan and installation commands in section 4
using the existing real hostname and certificate paths. Do not switch
to HTTP accidentally.

When using the installer-managed Nginx example, select --components both.
A partial update may omit the unselected application from the shared
proxy configuration and will be rejected.

6. INSTALLING OR UPGRADING ONLY ONE APPLICATION
-----------------------------------------------

In direct mode, select --components dxweb or --components admin.

DXWeb only:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components dxweb --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components dxweb --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider --apply

DXWeb Admin only:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action plan --root /spider \
    --components admin --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action install --root /spider \
    --components admin --mode direct --scheme http \
    --user sysop --group spider --apply

7. CHECKING THE INSTALLATION
----------------------------

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action status --components both
  systemctl is-active dxweb.service dxweb-admin.service
  systemctl status dxweb.service --no-pager
  systemctl status dxweb-admin.service --no-pager
  ss -lntp | grep -E ':(7380|7381|7480|7481)\b'

For direct HTTP installations:

  cd /spider
  curl -f http://127.0.0.1:7380/software-version.json
  curl -f http://127.0.0.1:7381/software-versions.json

For the Nginx HTTP example, replace the hostname:

  cd /spider
  nginx -t
  curl -f http://web.example.net:7380/software-version.json
  curl -f http://web.example.net:7381/software-versions.json

For the Nginx HTTPS example, use HTTPS and your actual hostname:

  cd /spider
  nginx -t
  curl -f https://web.example.net:7380/software-version.json
  curl -f https://web.example.net:7381/software-versions.json

Open both interfaces in a browser. Confirm that DXWeb receives spots
and that an authorized SYSOP can sign in to DXWeb Admin. Check the
supervision views and historical data. Verify that users without
administrative privileges cannot access administrative functions.

8. LOGS AND RECOVERY
--------------------

If a service fails, inspect its logs first:

  cd /spider
  journalctl -u dxweb.service -n 100 --no-pager
  journalctl -u dxweb-admin.service -n 100 --no-pager

For the Nginx example, also inspect:

  cd /spider
  journalctl -u nginx.service -n 100 --no-pager

The installer stores configuration transactions under:

  /var/backups/dxweb-installer/

List the available transaction directories:

  cd /spider
  ls -lt /var/backups/dxweb-installer/

To preview a rollback, replace REAL_TRANSACTION with the exact name
of an existing backup directory:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action rollback \
    --backup /var/backups/dxweb-installer/REAL_TRANSACTION

Only after reviewing the transaction, apply the rollback if needed:

  cd /spider
  perl dxweb/dxweb-manager.pl --action rollback \
    --backup /var/backups/dxweb-installer/REAL_TRANSACTION \
    --apply

Do not perform a rollback as a routine test. Do not delete databases,
filters, certificates, or local configuration. Configuration rollback
does not replace the Git-managed application source code.

9. COMMON ERRORS
----------------

Source bundle missing:
  The installer does not match the integrated Git layout. Do not fix
  this by downloading a separate installer bundle.

Symlink installation root forbidden:
  Check that /spider is the actual repository directory.

Existing DXWeb Nginx site:
  Preserve the existing configuration and plan its migration.

Partial Nginx update:
  Select --components both for the shared proxy configuration.

Health check failed:
  Check services, listening ports, and logs before retrying.

NO CHANGES:
  The generated configuration already matches the requested plan.
  Check services and application behavior before considering the
  installation complete.

